@startuml
title T12-WF02 — AI Lead Enrichment Agent (Sequence)
autonumber
participant "RabbitMQ" as MQ
participant "n8n WF02\nEnrichment" as N8N
participant "NestJS Backend" as API
database "PostgreSQL" as DB
participant "Mock Enrichment Adapter" as MOCK

MQ -> N8N: lead.enrichment.requested(eventId, leadId)
activate N8N
N8N -> N8N: Validate event and request IDs
N8N -> API: GET lead
API -> DB: Read authoritative lead data
DB --> API: Lead record
API --> N8N: Lead data
N8N -> N8N: Extract and normalize website/email domain
N8N -> MOCK: Lookup fixture by domain
MOCK --> N8N: Deterministic mock fields + providerMode=MOCK
N8N -> N8N: Normalize fields and validate completeness/provenance
alt All required fields available
N8N -> API: POST enrichment callback(status=SUCCESS, providerMode=MOCK)
else Some fields unavailable
N8N -> API: POST enrichment callback(status=PARTIAL, missingFields, providerMode=MOCK)
else Adapter/processing failure
N8N -> API: POST enrichment callback(status=FAILED, errorCode, providerMode=MOCK)
end
API -> DB: Persist enrichment result idempotently
DB --> API: Persisted status/result ID
API --> N8N: Callback accepted
opt PARTIAL or FAILED and owner notification is enabled
N8N -> API: Request backend notification
API -> DB: Record notification/audit status
API --> N8N: Notification request result
end
N8N -> N8N: Build summary with MOCK provenance and correlation IDs
deactivate N8N
note over MOCK,N8N
Mock data must be visibly labelled as demo/mock. No live provider
or external credentials are assumed in this baseline.
end note
@enduml
